OL,3,GNEWSAReopened waste site will not cut
OL,4,Afly-tipping, council told
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe re-opening of a Keighley waste
OL,7,Frecycling site was unlikely to cut the
OL,8,Famount of rubbish being fly-tipped as
OL,9,Fmost of it was being dumped by
OL,10,Forganised crime gangs and rogue
OL,11,Ftraders, councillors have been told.
OL,13,FBradford Council's executive voted in
OL,14,FSeptember to reopen the Sugden End
OL,15,FHousehold Waste Recycling Centre in
OL,16,FCross Roads after it was closed in
OL,17,F2024.
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
